1
00:00:01,310 --> 00:00:11,560
Right this way, Mr. and Mrs. Stewart.

2
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:14,430
Well, it's small, but clean.

3
00:00:14,430 --> 00:00:22,300
Clean? You call this clean?

4
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,230
Have a nice stay.

5
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:33,560
Thank you. I don't believe this.

6
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:40,060
Well, it isn't the Watermill Inn,

7
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:52,710
but let's get a look at the view.

8
00:00:52,710 --> 00:00:54,740
How is the view?

9
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:59,640
Great, if you enjoy looking at a parking lot.

10
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:03,700
Well, maybe we'll see the view in the morning.

11
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:21,850
Right now, we should clean up this room.

12
00:01:21,850 --> 00:01:24,240
Sorry, Marilyn.

13
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:26,630
Why should you be sorry?

14
00:01:26,630 --> 00:01:31,910
Well, the rain, the room, the view of the parking lot.

15
00:01:31,910 --> 00:01:34,960
It isn't the way I hoped it would be.

16
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:38,000
Stop blaming yourself.

17
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:45,470
After all, we're here, we're alone, we're together.

18
00:01:45,470 --> 00:01:49,940
And I love you. Isn't that enough?

19
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:50,800
It is for me,

20
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:55,500
but I wanted this weekend to be special for you.

21
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:05,610
It is special. Happy anniversary.

22
00:02:05,610 --> 00:02:09,060
It's still raining. I want to play tennis.

23
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:10,950
I want some breakfast.

24
00:02:10,950 --> 00:02:13,670
Let's call room service and order a nice breakfast,

25
00:02:13,670 --> 00:02:16,160
and then we'll figure out what to do today.

26
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:24,990
Right. Would you give me room service, please?

27
00:02:24,990 --> 00:02:34,450
I beg your pardon? Oh, I see.

28
00:02:34,450 --> 00:02:38,840
They don't have room service at Old Country Inn.

29
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:42,670
Well, let's go down to the coffee shop.

30
00:02:42,670 --> 00:02:45,110
They don't have a coffee shop.

31
00:02:45,110 --> 00:02:51,870
We can get our meals at Mrs. Montefiore's down the road.

32
00:02:51,870 --> 00:02:53,410
That's OK, honey.

33
00:02:53,410 --> 00:02:55,180
I love walking in the rain.

34
00:02:55,180 --> 00:02:58,990
Oh, you're being a really good sport about this, Marilyn,

35
00:02:58,990 --> 00:03:00,610
but I think we should face the truth.

36
00:03:00,610 --> 00:03:02,260
What's that?

37
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:05,610
This is not the way to spend our fifth anniversary.

38
00:03:05,610 --> 00:03:09,490
Well, what do you want to do?

39
00:03:09,490 --> 00:03:11,820
Why don't we get in the car and drive home?

40
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:15,330
Oh, Richard, it really isn't that bad.

41
00:03:15,330 --> 00:03:20,320
Do you want to stick it out for the whole weekend?

42
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:22,800
Well, I'll admit the room is uncomfortable.

43
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:25,000
Uh-hum.

44
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,700
And I do feel bad about your mother

45
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:30,310
having to take care of the baby all weekend.

46
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:31,750
Why don't we just check out?

47
00:03:31,750 --> 00:03:39,810
OK.

48
00:03:39,810 --> 00:03:44,550
Hello? Yes. Yes, this is she.

49
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:49,430
Oh, hello! How nice of you to remember us!

50
00:03:49,430 --> 00:03:52,550
Yes, my husband did call.

51
00:03:52,550 --> 00:03:58,980
You do? Really? It won't be any trouble?

52
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:04,430
Oh, yes, I think we'd like that very much.

53
00:04:04,430 --> 00:04:13,480
Fifteen minutes! Thank you. Good-bye.

54
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:15,880
You will never guess.

55
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:18,690
Uh ... I give up.

56
00:04:18,690 --> 00:04:24,150
Mrs. Montefiore from the Watermill Inn.

57
00:04:24,150 --> 00:04:26,770
What is she calling about?

58
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:28,430
They have an opening.

59
00:04:28,430 --> 00:04:29,730
Someone just checked out.

60
00:04:29,730 --> 00:04:34,180
and Mrs. Montefiore has reserved the honeymoon suite for us.

61
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:34,850
You're kidding!

62
00:04:34,850 --> 00:04:37,300
No. Isn't it wonderful?

63
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:38,800
It's fantastic!

64
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:43,450
Oh. Now all it has to do is stop raining.

65
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:46,450
Let's go.
